packets.implementation:
DESIGN: defer, do not reorder. Reordering (collect_routes_in before collect_calls_in) would also work, but it moves every route file's ENDPOINT / GORM / DI pushes behind its ROUTE pushes, reordering acc.nodes / acc.refs for files that have no closure at all. Deferral appends closure CallSites after the existing ones, so a file without a func literal parses to a byte-identical FileParse.
1. `fn collect_calls_in<'t>(node: TsNode<'t>, src, from, receiver_var, repo, file_rel, acc, pending: &mut Vec<TsNode<'t>>)`: for a child of kind func_literal push it onto `pending` and do not recurse; everything else unchanged (the three detectors try_detect_go_endpoint / try_detect_gorm_access / try_detect_go_provider_set still run on each call_expression).
2. `fn collect_closure_calls(pending: Vec<TsNode>, src, from, receiver_var, repo, file_rel, acc)` called by visit_function / visit_method right after collect_routes_in: `while let Some(lit) = queue.pop_front()` (VecDeque, source order): if `acc.func_literal_handlers.contains(&lit.start_byte())` { acc.route_literals_skipped += 1; continue } - the literal is a route handler whose callees LA.18d already made HANDLED_BY refs, and nothing nested in it is attributed (LA.18d's rule: the registering function is not the handler). Else acc.closure_bodies += 1 and walk `lit.child_by_field_name("body")` with collect_calls_in(.., same from, same receiver_var, &mut next) and extend the queue with `next`. closure_calls counts the CallSites pushed while draining (acc.calls.len() before / after).
3. Semantics: every call inside a non-route closure is a CallSite `from` the enclosing FUNCTION / METHOD at the call's own row (LC.3b site line); the receiver_var carries into the closure, so `s.init()` in `once.Do(func() { s.init() })` is SelfMethod. A client ENDPOINT, GORM access or wire.Build inside a goroutine is attributed to the enclosing function as well. Unchanged: package-level `var f = func() {..}` (not a function body; no calls collected today), route-handler literals and everything nested in them. A queue / cron callback literal (`nc.Subscribe("x", func(m) { onX(m) })`) is not a Go-parser route, so its callees become CALLS of the registering function in addition to the extractor's HANDLED_BY (LA.33): declared in risks.
4. Marker, per file, only when closure_bodies + route_literals_skipped > 0, printed after the `[go-routes]` func-literal line: `[go-calls] func-literal bodies=<b> calls=<c> route-literal bodies skipped=<r> in <file>`.
5. Tests (parsers/code/go/src/lib.rs):
(a) closure_calls_belong_to_the_enclosing_function - the fixture's app.go: calls from `app::Provider` contain Bare("NewRepo") with line == the 0-based row of `repo = NewRepo()`; calls from `app::Start` contain Bare("worker"), Bare("cleanup"), Bare("flush") (go func / defer func / g.Go);
(b) route_literal_callees_are_not_calls_of_the_registrar - same source: no CallSite from `app::Routes` names "writeHealth"; handled_by(route ANY /health) == [bare("writeHealth")] (LA.18d unchanged);
(c) nested_closures_are_walked - `func Run() { go func() { defer func() { flush() }() }() }` -> Bare("flush") from Run;
(d) method_closure_keeps_the_receiver - `func (s *Svc) Boot() { once.Do(func() { s.init() }) }` -> SelfMethod("init") from `<pkg>::Svc::Boot`;
(e) extend nested_func_literal_calls_are_not_refs: additionally assert no CallSite from main::main names cleanup, background or serve (all inside the route literal).
engine/tests/call_site_lines.rs go_closure_call_carries_its_site_line: files go.mod + main.go `func local() int { return 2 }` and `func run() { var once sync.Once\n once.Do(func() {\n  local()\n }) }`; generate_one -> exactly one CALLS edge run -> local, its EVIDENCE basis Site and its line's source text contains `local()` (the closure row, not run's declaration row).

