packets.implementation:
WHERE: inside GoPackages (graph/src/build.rs), the extra_hook, so it runs only after every generic lookup (import binding, module symbol, A6.2a receiver type) missed: an edge that resolves today keeps its target and evidence.
`fn resolve(&self, g, site) -> Option<(NodeId, Evidence)> { self.package_call(g, site).or_else(|| self.typed_receiver(g, site)) }` - package_call is today's body with its `?`s now local to it.
RECEIVER: Attribute{base, name} -> chain [Ident(base)]; ComplexReceiver{receiver, name} -> parse CA.2a's chain text on `.` into segments `Ident(s)` / `Call(s)` (a segment ending in `()`); a receiver that does not parse (raw fallback text with brackets, quotes, spaces) -> None. Method name may be lower-case (same-package methods).
TYPE WALK `fn chain_type(g, caller_fn, caller_module, segs, depth) -> Option<(NodeId /*type*/, Source)>`, at most 6 segments and recursion depth 4:
- root Ident("self") -> enclosing_class_or_struct(caller_fn) (Source::FieldChain once a field follows);
- root Ident(x) with a local: g.nav.local_types[caller_fn][x] ("" -> None) -> type_of_text(text, caller_module) (Source::Local);
- root Ident(x) naming an import of caller_module (import_path) -> package context dir = imported_dir(..);
- root Ident(x) as a package var: local_types[m][x] for the MODULE scopes m of the caller's package dir (by_dir), exactly one distinct text -> type_of_text(text, m) (Source::PackageVar);
- root Call(f) -> the Bare function f through the caller module's symbols, then unique_in(caller dir, f); its return_types entry -> type_of_text(ret, callee module) (Source::Return);
- package context + Call(F) -> unique_in(dir, F): a FUNCTION -> its return type (Source::Return); a STRUCT / INTERFACE -> that type itself (a conversion `pkg.T(x)`, Source::Return); package context + Ident(V) -> a package var of that dir as above;
- type T + Ident(f) -> field_types[T][f] (bare, LA.23c) -> unique_type_in(dir of T, name) else unique_global_type(name) (Source::FieldChain);
- type T + Call(m) -> class_methods[T][m] or interface_methods[T][m] -> its return type in the method's module (Source::Return).
`fn type_of_text(text, ctx_module)`: ends in `()` -> re-parse it as a chain rooted in ctx_module (depth+1); `pkg.T` -> imported_dir(g, ctx_module, pkg) -> unique_type_in(dir, T); `T` -> unique_type_in(dir of ctx_module, T), else unique_global_type(T). unique_type_in / unique_global_type accept only STRUCT / INTERFACE (Go) - STRUCT / CLASS / INTERFACE / ENUM for the calls.rs helper - so the quokka FUNCTION `UserRepository` never answers a type lookup; two distinct answers -> None (never first-wins).
FINAL: class_methods[T][name], else interface_methods[T][name] (an interface-typed receiver binds the interface METHOD; A6.6's method-level IMPLEMENTS carries on to the implementations, as for the generic pass). Evidence go_ev(rule) with rule receiver_return | receiver_local | receiver_package_var | receiver_field_chain (the Source of the LAST hop), line = site line (resolve_calls attaches it). A test file's package vars / types answer only a test caller (the unique_in `with_tests` rule).
MARKER, once per Go graph, from Cell counters: `[go-receivers] bound=<n> (return=<a> local=<b> package_var=<c> field_chain=<d>) typed_unbound=<u>` where typed_unbound counts sites whose receiver had a recorded type text but whose type or method did not resolve.
calls.rs: `pub(crate) fn unique_global_type(g, name)` beside unique_global_function; resolve_type_name (the generic A6.2a chain) is NOT changed, so no other language's CALLS move.
TESTS: graph/tests/go_typed_receivers.rs (new) parses each file with glia_parser_go::parse_file the way graph/tests/go_package_dir.rs does (module qname = path minus `.go`, `/` -> `::`), so CA.2a's recorded facts are exercised end to end: go_typed_receiver_fixture (the bench fixture's five files: the four expected CALLS present, the three OrderRepository CALLS absent, evidence emitter graph:go_packages with rules receiver_return / receiver_local / receiver_local / receiver_package_var); go_typed_receiver_field_chain (`func (s *Svc) Run() { s.deps.repo.Save() }` through two field types, rule receiver_field_chain); go_typed_receiver_kind_filter (a FUNCTION and a STRUCT share the name `UserRepository`: the STRUCT answers); go_typed_receiver_conversion (`repositories.UserRepository(x).Save()`); go_typed_receiver_ambiguous (two STRUCTs of the name in two dirs, a bare unimported type text -> no edge); go_typed_receiver_keeps_generic_hits (a same-file `u *User` parameter binds through the generic pass, evidence graph:calls rule receiver_type, not the hook). graph/src/build.rs mod tests receiver_tally_marker_shape: fixed counters -> `[go-receivers] bound=7 (return=3 local=2 package_var=1 field_chain=1) typed_unbound=2`.

