```rust
// engine/src/diff_impact.rs
/// The impact of an already computed rev delta (module docs: rev mode). Nothing is built.
pub fn diff_impact_from_delta(rev: &RevDelta, opts: &BlastOptions) -> DiffImpact
pub fn diff_impact_vs_rev(repo_path: &str, base: &str, opts: &BlastOptions) -> Result<DiffImpact, String> {
    let rev = graph_delta_vs_rev(repo_path, base)?;
    Ok(diff_impact_from_delta(&rev, opts))
}
// engine/src/tests_for.rs
/// The tests for an already computed rev delta (module docs). `Err` beyond MAX_SEEDS seeds only.
pub fn tests_for_delta(rev: &RevDelta, args: &TestsForArgs) -> Result<TestsFor, String>
pub fn tests_for_rev(repo_path: &str, base: &str, args: &TestsForArgs) -> Result<TestsFor, String> {
    let rev = crate::delta::graph_delta_vs_rev(repo_path, base)?;
    tests_for_delta(&rev, args)
}
```
The base label both answers carry is `rev.answer.base` (graph_delta_vs_rev stores the rev AS GIVEN there, delta.rs GraphDeltaAnswer { base: rev.given }), so `DiffImpact.base`, the absence query `rev <base>` and the `[diff-impact] mode=rev base=<base>` marker are byte-identical to today's. diff_impact_from_delta keeps `impact.absence.unparsed_files = rev.after.parse_errors.len()`. The `_delta` names mirror patterns::pattern_conformance_delta (a function of an already computed delta); `from_` matches diff_impact_from_diff. Module docs of both files gain one paragraph naming the new entry and the one-delta use (a caller answering impact AND tests builds once). No CLI / pyo3 change: their `--base` / `*_rev` paths keep calling the wrappers (CC-3's review is the first two-answer caller).

