from_source: build `Adjacency::build(g, &CategorySet::of(<categories with weight > 0>))`, then walk each node's outgoing incidences and add `weight(category)` to the UNORDERED pair (min, max); a self-loop adds to self_w (counted twice in strength, the modularity convention). Parallel and opposite edges sum. The dense order is the node ids sorted by NodeId.0 (dangling endpoints of kept edges included), so the view is a pure function of the edge SET: permuting the source's node or edge order cannot change it. Accumulate pairs in a Vec<(u32,u32,u64)>, sort, merge - no HashMap iteration anywhere (the only map is Adjacency's lookup index). modularity: Q = sum_c [ in_c / 2m - (num/den) * (K_c / 2m)^2 ] computed from u64/u128 sums, converted to f64 once at the end (display only; every decision in CD.1b compares integers). label_propagation: labels = dense index; each round visits nodes in a SplitMix64(seed) Fisher-Yates order of 0..n; a node takes the label with the largest summed edge weight among its neighbours (ties: the smallest label; staying put wins a tie with the current label); stops after a round with no change or max_rounds. Final membership renumbered by (community size desc, smallest member NodeId asc) so ids are canonical. Isolated nodes (strength 0) stay singletons. u32 dense indices follow LD.15's cap (over-limit input returns an empty view, never a panic).

