`pub fn scip_dir(root: &Path) -> PathBuf` = root/.glia/scip-snapshot (CONTROL_DIR joined, as history_dir). `pub fn source_hash(bytes: &[u8]) -> String` = data_hash(&[bytes]) - one definition so the importer and the build stage agree. `pub fn write_scip(root, meta: ScipMeta, documents: &[ScipDocumentRecord], symbols: &[ScipSymbolRecord]) -> Result<ScipMeta, String>`: returns Err (nothing written) unless documents are strictly sorted by path, symbols strictly by id with ids 0..n, every row's `s` and every `implements` id < n, and each document's defs / refs sorted by (line, s, flags) - a caller bug can never write an order-dependent snapshot; creates the dir, removes an existing meta.json FIRST (as write_history, so a write that stops part-way leaves a snapshot read_scip rejects), serialises documents.jsonl then symbols.jsonl through jsonl, write_atomic each, sets meta.documents / symbols to the row counts and meta.data_hash = data_hash(&[docs_bytes, syms_bytes]), writes meta.json LAST through write_atomic and returns the meta as written. It prints nothing and writes no .gitignore (the importer, CE.1b, owns both, as history_sync does for write_history). `pub fn read_scip(root) -> Option<ScipSnapshot>`: None silently when the dir is absent; when present but meta.json is missing / unparsable / of another version, the data does not hash to meta.data_hash, a row does not parse, or a row count differs from the meta, prints `[scip] snapshot incomplete dir=<dir> reason=<reason>` once and returns None (read_history's contract). No redaction: the snapshot holds indexer-generated symbol strings, identifier text sliced at definition ranges and line numbers - no free text and no values.

