packets.implementation:
DESIGN: an abstract class is a class for every consumer (it is extended, injected, decorated and calls its own members), so it takes visit_class unchanged; an abstract member is a METHOD without a body (it is called as `this.m()`, overridden and implemented), exactly CB.9's rule for a Dart bodiless member. No new kind, category, cell or NavFact. Alternatives weighed: a new node kind (needs a registry id and splits every METHOD consumer, e.g. `implementors` answers METHOD targets through the owner); an ATTRIBUTE (wrong: it is callable and `this.fetchOne()` must bind to it); recording abstract-ness (no reader in this batch: inherited-call / abstract-override resolution is a recorded gap, so a fact now would be write-only).
1. visit_top: `"class_declaration" | "abstract_class_declaration" => visit_class(n, ..)`. visit_class reads `name`, `body`, the class_heritage child and the decorators through names both kinds share, so class_di_shape / class_decorators (which also reads the parent export_statement's decorators) / collect_constructor_injects / collect_ctor_param_field_types / emit_typeorm_entity / collect_class_heritage take the node as is. `declare abstract class` (an ambient_declaration) still falls through, as `declare class` does.
2. visit_class: the CG.1 pre-scan filter becomes `matches!(m.kind(), "method_definition" | "abstract_method_signature")` so a function-valued field named like an abstract member is counted shadowed, not minted twice. Member match gains `"abstract_method_signature" => visit_abstract_method(member, src, file_rel, &class_qname, class_id, repo, acc)`. `method_signature` (an overload signature, plain or abstract class) stays ignored: the implementation that follows carries the node. When `n.kind() == "abstract_class_declaration"`: acc.abstract_stats.classes += 1.
3. `fn visit_abstract_method(n, src, file_rel, class_qname, class_id, repo, acc)`: name node = n.child_by_field_name("name"), kind property_identifier or private_property_identifier only (a computed / string / number name mints nothing, as CG.1); if acc.class_methods already holds (class_id, name) return (a repeated signature keeps one NodeId); method_qname = `{class_qname}::{name}`; method_id = NodeId::from_parts(GRAPH_TYPE, repo, METHOD, &method_qname); push Node { confidence: Strong, cells: build_cells_from(&n, first_decorator(n), src, file_rel) } (CB.4's rule: a member's decorators are class_body siblings); DEFINES class -> method with empty cells (the engine stamps `parser:<tag>` like visit_method's); class_methods.insert((class_id, name), method_id) so `this.fetchOne()` binds in resolve_intra_file as SelfMethod -> intra_file CALLS with the call row (LC.3b); nav.record(method_id, name, &method_qname, METHOD, Some(class_id)); abstract_stats.methods += 1. No body, so no call walk; parameters are not walked (visit_method walks only collect_inject_repository over them, which an abstract signature never carries).
4. collect_calls_in: the skip list `function_declaration | method_definition | class_declaration | class_expression` gains `abstract_class_declaration`, so a class declared inside a body is skipped whichever keyword it has.
5. angular.rs extract_class_name: `line.trim_start_matches("export ").trim_start_matches("default ").trim_start_matches("abstract ")`, then `class `. Fixes find_next_class_name (decorator -> class) and the `*Guard` convention scan alike; the doc at :132 becomes true.
6. Marker, in parse_file_stats after the `[ts-fields]` line, when classes + methods > 0: `[ts-abstract] classes=<c> abstract_methods=<m> file=<file_rel>`.
7. TESTS (parsers/code/typescript/src/lib.rs mod tests, repo() / id() / has_node helpers): (a) abstract_class_is_a_class_with_methods - `export abstract class BaseRepo<T> {
  protected load(id: string): T {
    return this.fetchOne(id);
  }
  abstract fetchOne(id: string): T;
  protected abstract label(): string;
  describe(): string {
    return this.label();
  }
}` in src/base-repo.ts: CLASS src::base-repo::BaseRepo; METHODs load / fetchOne / label / describe; DEFINES class -> fetchOne; intra_file CALLS load -> fetchOne whose Evidence line is 2 and describe -> label (line 7); fetchOne's CODE is `abstract fetchOne(id: string): T;` and its POSITION start_line 4; no CallSite from fetchOne. (b) unexported_and_default_abstract - `abstract class A { abstract run(): void; }` and `export default abstract class B { go() {} }` mint CLASS A (+ METHOD run) and CLASS B (+ METHOD go); `[ts-abstract]` counters through parse_file_stats read classes=2 methods=1. (c) abstract_heritage_refs - `export abstract class Repo extends Base implements IRepo {}` emits INHERITS_FROM Bare("Base") and IMPLEMENTS Bare("IRepo") refs from Repo. (d) decorated_abstract_service_injects - `import { Injectable } from '@angular/core';
@Injectable()
export abstract class S {
  constructor(private p: ProductService) {}
}` emits the INJECTS ref Bare("ProductService") from S (DiShape::TsCtor). parsers/code/extractors/src/angular.rs mod tests: (e) abstract_class_after_decorator_is_named - `@Injectable()
export abstract class FilterDataService {}` yields ("FilterDataService", SERVICE) and `@Directive()
abstract class AnalyticsDirective {}` yields ("AnalyticsDirective", DIRECTIVE) from scan_decorated_classes (the function the existing detects_* tests reach through extract_angular_nodes).

